Independently usable source subtrees, and the components Lege links from the
sibling exprim repository, retain the license declared by their own Cargo
manifest and license files. In particular:

- ../exprim (the PDF engine): MIT, with PDFium's BSD-3-Clause notice for its
  bundled font faces and Unicode data (see its THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md)
- ../exprim/codecs/djvulibrust: AGPL-3.0-only
- ../exprim/codecs/jbig2enc-rust: MIT project contributions and Apache-2.0 retained
  arithmetic-coder components (MIT AND Apache-2.0). The DjVu-derived component
  implementation has been replaced; see its PROVENANCE.md and NOTICE.
- ../exprim/codecs/jp2lam: MIT OR Apache-2.0
- lege-process/GUI/rfd: MIT
- lege-process/GUI/liminalUI/fonts/Inter-Regular.ttf: OFL-1.1 (see OFL.txt
  beside it)
- lege-pdf/pdf-integrity and other explicitly licensed PDF components: the
  licenses declared in their own manifests and source notices

Third-party dependencies, models, and derived compatibility portions retain
their own copyrights, licenses, and attribution requirements. The release
notice presented to users is maintained in lege-misc/docs/licenses.html.

The source audit and unresolved declarations are recorded in
docs/LICENSING-AUDIT.md. This map does not relicense inherited third-party code.
